A||||3||Lewis||Swapping 85gt 6cyl into 88 coupe-4cyl both auto||||5||
Z||000000||Lewis||03-03-2001||09:30 PM||||Can someone tell me how hard it is to swap a 6cyl into a 88 coupe that has a 4cyl in it. Both cars are automatics..want to know if it is worth the time and money..looking for some advice..the 6cyl is in a 85gt..<BR>thanks..||||reg||5
Z||000001||ray b||03-04-2001||12:15 AM|||| not to hard was done to my 88 before I got it. fuel pump is the worst got to drop tank,for it.don't forget the radeator v6 is<BR> 2 core.4 cly only 1 core. replace EMC,wires, tack, ect with v6 cars parts.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||03-04-2001||12:21 AM||||I'm in need of parts off the 4 cyl if you are scrapping it. I especially want the chip from the ECM for another project I'm working on along side the brakes.<P>since you have both cars, the project isn't hard, but it will eat a huge amount of time.||||reg||1
Z||000003||TheFiero64||03-04-2001||10:21 AM||||It didn't take me long at all. You will have to trim a couple of inches off the coolant pipe that runs along the back of the V6 to clear the 88 suspension. You will see this when you mount the engine on the cradle. You will also have to drill 2 new bolt holes in the cradle for the front engine mount if you are not using an 88 front mount. Like Ray b said the Fuel pump is the hardest part. <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
